From 901b9b5a33f49505500c4279c755d8b111619bd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zonglvye <zonglvye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:46:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 82/97] fix(playback): make the progress bar work for streamed
 audio

The bar was dead on streamed tracks: no total, no fill, no seeking. Three causes,
all in the MSE path, plus the missing fallback:

- appendBuffer throws QuotaExceededError *synchronously* when the buffer quota is
  exhausted, and that throw ended the whole append loop (logged as
  'streaming append failed'). Everything after it never reached the buffer, so
  endOfStream() never ran and the element kept reporting duration === Infinity
  for the life of the track. Now the synchronous throw is caught, the oldest half
  of the buffered range is evicted, and the chunk is retried.
- the pump also appended the entire file as fast as it arrived, which is what
  filled the quota. It now waits while it is more than 30 s ahead of the playhead
  (a paused deck therefore buffers 30 s and stops instead of the whole track).
- duration Infinity also means the lock screen gets no position state. The track
  knows its own length, so materializeShellAudioSource now takes it and sets
  mediaSource.duration before the first append; the element reports a finite
  length from the start instead of waiting for endOfStream.
- onLoadedMetadata falls back to SongResult.durationMs when the element still
  says Infinity, so a slow start cannot leave the bar without a total.

Verified on the device: 04:33 total from the first frame, the fill tracks
playback, tapping the bar seeks (02:51 at a 44% tap) and keeps playing, buffered
stays around 35 s ahead, and no further quota failures in the log.
